and marketing businesses

00:00:46.450 --> 00:00:51.430
by helping them unleash their
data or the power of their data

00:00:51.430 --> 00:00:55.400
using our AI and big data
processing technologies.

00:00:55.400 --> 00:00:58.130
MAX SALTONSTALL: So I'm
using an app on my phone,

00:00:58.130 --> 00:01:00.700
I see an ad inviting me
to install something else.

00:01:00.700 --> 00:01:02.470
Can you walk me
through the lifecycle

00:01:02.470 --> 00:01:05.860
of how that ad gets through
all of these systems

00:01:05.860 --> 00:01:07.810
and ends up on my screen?

00:01:07.810 --> 00:01:10.090
CHANG KIM: We start working
with our customers, who

00:01:10.090 --> 00:01:14.800
are typically mobile app
development companies,

00:01:14.800 --> 00:01:16.930
and then their marketing
teams come to us

00:01:16.930 --> 00:01:19.900
and then commission their
advertisement campaigns

00:01:19.900 --> 00:01:23.140
because they wanted
to sell their apps

00:01:23.140 --> 00:01:26.510
or have more people use their
apps, install their apps,

00:01:26.510 --> 00:01:28.360
engage with their
apps, and so on.

00:01:28.360 --> 00:01:32.500
So that's their key goal that
they achieve through MOLOCO.

00:01:32.500 --> 00:01:36.140
And when we receive these ad
campaigns, on the other hand,

00:01:36.140 --> 00:01:39.970
we have lots of
mobile users out there

00:01:39.970 --> 00:01:45.280
around the world, billions of
users using phones or typically

00:01:45.280 --> 00:01:48.830
similar kind of form
factors, tablets and so on.

00:01:48.830 --> 00:01:52.960
So whenever they use their
devices, some apps are running

00:01:52.960 --> 00:01:56.290
and then these apps keep
creating the advertisement

00:01:56.290 --> 00:01:57.640
slots.

00:01:57.640 --> 00:02:01.660
So these are called ad
spaces or ad inventories,

00:02:01.660 --> 00:02:05.800
and then we basically want
to field these ad inventories

00:02:05.800 --> 00:02:09.729
by showing them the most
relevant and helpful

00:02:09.729 --> 00:02:13.550
advertisement contents to them.

00:02:13.550 --> 00:02:16.330
And to do that, we
need some matchmaking

00:02:16.330 --> 00:02:18.010
and then this
matchmaking is done

00:02:18.010 --> 00:02:21.610
through what we call the
advertisement exchanges or ad

00:02:21.610 --> 00:02:22.720
exchanges.

00:02:22.720 --> 00:02:27.220
These are similar to the stock
exchanges like NYSE and NASDAQ

00:02:27.220 --> 00:02:31.240
where supply and demand meet
together and then arrive

00:02:31.240 --> 00:02:35.560
at the right outcomes
through online bidding.

00:02:35.560 --> 00:02:39.320
We receive these ad
inventories not directly,

00:02:39.320 --> 00:02:40.960
but through ad exchanges.

00:02:40.960 --> 00:02:44.200
And then whenever we
receive this bid request,

00:02:44.200 --> 00:02:49.630
we quickly evaluate the
value of this ad space

00:02:49.630 --> 00:02:54.670
relative to our advertisement
customers campaigns

00:02:54.670 --> 00:02:57.310
and then we use a lot of big
data and machine learning

00:02:57.310 --> 00:03:00.520
technologies to make a
decision on whether we

00:03:00.520 --> 00:03:04.070
should participate in that
bidding or we should not.

00:03:04.070 --> 00:03:06.820
And then if we're going to
participate, at what price

00:03:06.820 --> 00:03:08.510
should we bid for?

00:03:08.510 --> 00:03:09.010
Right?

00:03:09.010 --> 00:03:12.400
So we make these quick
computations and decisions

00:03:12.400 --> 00:03:17.140
and then when we respond,
again, back to the ad exchanges,

00:03:17.140 --> 00:03:19.420
the exchanges collect
this information

00:03:19.420 --> 00:03:21.640
and then run the
auction, online auction.

00:03:21.640 --> 00:03:24.850
And then if we happen
to win, then we

00:03:24.850 --> 00:03:29.050
own that particular ad space
that is created at that point

00:03:29.050 --> 00:03:33.770
and then we show our customers
ads through that space.

00:03:33.770 --> 00:03:36.220
So the unique thing
about this industry

00:03:36.220 --> 00:03:38.410
and using ML for
this industry is

00:03:38.410 --> 00:03:42.100
that we have to come up
with quality inference

00:03:42.100 --> 00:03:47.560
result, but very timely as well
because think about the stock

00:03:47.560 --> 00:03:48.340
exchange, right?

00:03:48.340 --> 00:03:51.010
When you announce that
there is this supply,

00:03:51.010 --> 00:03:53.530
the demand has to make
a bid very quickly.

00:03:53.530 --> 00:03:58.540
In online ad, the
strictness of the time

00:03:58.540 --> 00:04:02.860
is actually even harsher because
when you open a publishing app,

00:04:02.860 --> 00:04:05.530
that ad slot doesn't
wait for you forever.

00:04:05.530 --> 00:04:09.760
It's usually going to wait for,
say, about 100 milliseconds

00:04:09.760 --> 00:04:11.530
or 150 milliseconds.

00:04:11.530 --> 00:04:14.300
Within that or after
that, the proper ads

00:04:14.300 --> 00:04:18.048
need to show up otherwise
it's considered a failure.

00:04:18.048 --> 00:04:21.940
So when we receive these
bid requests through the ad

00:04:21.940 --> 00:04:25.480
exchanges we have to make
that decision very quickly,

00:04:25.480 --> 00:04:27.670
typically within
100 milliseconds.

00:04:27.670 --> 00:04:31.330
And then that 100 milliseconds
includes networking latency

00:04:31.330 --> 00:04:34.700
and our other infrastructure
latencies as well.

00:04:34.700 --> 00:04:38.980
So the actual amount of time
that is left for ML inference

00:04:38.980 --> 00:04:40.240
is actually even smaller.

00:04:40.240 --> 00:04:43.210
It's typically about 20
milliseconds or even less

00:04:43.210 --> 00:04:49.180
sometimes, but still we have to
make a very relevant prediction

00:04:49.180 --> 00:04:53.530
about this particular
user and the content

00:04:53.530 --> 00:04:57.700
and also we have to use many ML
models, not just one because we

00:04:57.700 --> 00:05:01.840
have to guess the, say,
the user's interest

00:05:01.840 --> 00:05:05.200
level about these
campaigns, many campaigns.

00:05:05.200 --> 00:05:09.370
And then we have to predict
how likely the user is going

00:05:09.370 --> 00:05:13.150
to use this app or they
respond to the advertisement

00:05:13.150 --> 00:05:15.730
and then use the
new app over time

00:05:15.730 --> 00:05:18.620
and then create even
more lifetime value.

00:05:18.620 --> 00:05:21.190
We also have to predict
the market conditions

00:05:21.190 --> 00:05:22.990
at that point in time
because everything

00:05:22.990 --> 00:05:26.050
keeps changing so that we
can derive the right bid

00:05:26.050 --> 00:05:27.200
price as well.

00:05:27.200 --> 00:05:31.750
So all these models need to work
together sometimes in tandem

00:05:31.750 --> 00:05:35.270
and then we still have to meet
the 20 millisecond latency.

00:05:35.270 --> 00:05:38.470
So that's the crux of
technical challenge

00:05:38.470 --> 00:05:40.010
that we're dealing with.

00:05:40.010 --> 00:05:43.132
And so we use a few--

00:05:43.132 --> 00:05:46.060
we learned a few lessons
by working in this industry

00:05:46.060 --> 00:05:48.410
long enough and then
creating values.

00:05:48.410 --> 00:05:55.930
So for example, we are using a
relatively shallow DNN model,

00:05:55.930 --> 00:05:57.440
so it's not that deep.

00:05:57.440 --> 00:06:00.640
And we realize that unlike
natural language processing

00:06:00.640 --> 00:06:03.910
or image processing,
these inferences that we

00:06:03.910 --> 00:06:06.730
make for this
advertisement businesses

00:06:06.730 --> 00:06:08.710
doesn't need to be
that deep, but we still

00:06:08.710 --> 00:06:10.220
use a lot of features.

00:06:10.220 --> 00:06:15.790
So it's shallow, but very,
very wide models that we use.

00:06:15.790 --> 00:06:19.120
And it's OK for us to spend
a lot more time and resources

00:06:19.120 --> 00:06:22.060
for training these big
but shallow models,

00:06:22.060 --> 00:06:24.590
but the inference needs
to be done very quickly.

00:06:24.590 --> 00:06:26.680
That's why we're
using shallow models.

00:06:26.680 --> 00:06:30.580
We're using a lot of other big
data processing technologies

00:06:30.580 --> 00:06:34.010
to reduce our response
time as much as possible,

00:06:34.010 --> 00:06:37.565
but I guess that probably
requires another session.

00:06:37.565 --> 00:06:38.440
MAX SALTONSTALL: Wow.

00:06:38.440 --> 00:06:40.660
Those are some
impressive numbers--

00:06:40.660 --> 00:06:42.310
